== Objective

The objective of this lab is to study the magnetic fields created by a solenoid
by mapping the field and measuring the magnetic field within a solenoid.

== Theory

When a coil of wire has an electric charge run through it, it generates a
magnetic field.  This charged coil is called a solenoid.  The strength of the
field in the middle of a solenoid can be measured by $
B = N/L mu_0 i
$ where $N$ is the number of turns, $L$ is the length of the coil and $mu_0 = 4
pi 10^(-7)$.

== Procedure

=== Procedure A

Setup a solenoid connected to the power supply.  Using a small compass, trace
the north/south pole to draw the lines of the magnetic field.

=== Procedure B

Attach a slinky to the table, stretched to a length of one metre.  Insert the
magnetic probe and attach the power supply to each end of the slinky.  After
recording data for a few seconds, turn on the power supply, wait a few seconds,
then turn it back off.

=== Procedure C

Using the same setup from Procedure B, set the current to 0.2 A.  Storing the
runs between, measure the magnetic field 5 times, recording the average and
standard deviation each time.

