== Analysis

=== Procedure B

The average value collected in Logger Pro was 0.000055 T.  Using the formula
discussed in the theory section, we can calcualte the theoretical $mu_0$ at
0.000050 T.  This gives us an error of #proc_err(.00005, .000055)

=== Procedure C

Using the data collected from proc c, we can plot the $N/L i$ vs the average B
field, giving us the following graph:

#image("./proc-c-anal.png")

Getting the slope and standard deviation of the slope using the provided table,
we get that the $mu_0 = 0.0000013 plus.minus 0.00098$

The theoretical $mu_0$ is $0.000001257$, giving us a #proc_err(0.000001257,
.0000013) error.

== Conclusion

In conclusion, we were able to visualse and measure the effects of a magnetic
field generated by a solenoid.

As with any experiment, there are errors.  The power supply, in this case, is
very prone to error as its values constantly change.  There is a chance that we
bumped it between setting it to a value and mesuring the result.

